language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Place n queens on an n x n chessboard so that no two queens share a row, column or diagonal.
given n : int(1..)
find queens : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)

branching on [queens]

such that
$ no two queens share a column
allDiff(queens),
$ no two queens share an ascending diagonal
allDiff([queens[i] + i | i : int(1..n)]),
$ no two queens share a descending diagonal
allDiff([queens[i] - i | i : int(1..n)])
